"Benjie Gandionco" <benjieg@corp.nsc.com>:
 >What is the /proc file system.  When I backup the / and /usr file systems,
 >this always gives me an error on /proc.

man procfs (on FreeBSD) tells me:
'The process file system, or, implements a view of the system process
 table inside the file system.'

It's an API (more or less) to certain parts of kernel-memory, which you
can use (providing your OS has a decent /proc implementation. Linux has
one) to find out about the things your OS is running.

Since this is a dynamically-generated filesystem, you can get errors when
you try to back it up, and therefore, it's wise to skip it during backups.

                                                                robert 



