Mathew E Goldstein wrote:
> 
> clos@ivory.trentu.ca wrote:
> 
> : I have tried the following aliases in my .profile but with out success:
> :
> :            alias p='PS1=`hostname|cut -d. -f1`":$PWD#"'
> :            alias cd='cd \!* ; p'

You don't need an alias at all, just do this:

PS1="\$PWD# "

The important thing is the \ before $PWD, it forces the shell
to re-evaluate $PWD each time the prompt is printed.

BTW, I don't like the "#" in your prompt, it looks too much like
a root prompt. Personally, I use 
PS1="`hostname`:`whoami` \$PWD> "

BTW2, you should put all alias and prompt settings in a
.kshrc file, and just

ENV=$HOME/.kshrc; export ENV

in .profile.


Roland Kruse



