Benjie Gandionco wrote:
> 
> How can I use a login other than root to backup and restore?  If I don't
> use root, some files are inaccessible and always gives out an error.   I
> don't want to give the root account to the guys in charge of backup for
> security purposes.

You could, depending on your backup software, make the software setuid
root. Then make it group but not world executable.
Put the guys who do the backups into an appropriate group, and make the
backup software the same group. If necessary, create a new group for
this.
Now your backup guys can run the backup software as root, but normal
users can't.

Alternatively, use 'sudo' to allow only specific people to run the
software.

Cheers,

Matt
