In article <E1L35C.9Ms@atww.org>, rshwake@atww.org (Raymond N Shwake) writes:
> clos@ivory.trentu.ca writes:
> 
>>We are using Korn shell (/bin/ksh) and I would like to have the shell display 
>>my present working directory ($PWD) in my command prompt evertime I "cd" to a
>>different directory. I have tried the following aliases in my .profile but with
>>out success:
>> 
>>           alias p='PS1=`hostname|cut -d. -f1`":$PWD#"'
>>           alias cd='cd \!* ; p'

 You could always define a shell function in your .profile as,

    cdp () {
        cd $*
        PS1="`hostname|cut -f1 -d.`:`basename $PWD`> "
    }

    alias cd=cdp

 Just a reminder that you can display ksh funtions using the 'typeset -f'
 command. :)

