From Ultrix domainname manpage:  (note 'yp' is old name for NIS)
   Domains are only used by the yellow pages (YP) service and are called
YP
   domains.  A YP domain is a directory in /etc/yp, established through
the
   use of the domainname command, ...

From SCO domainname manpage:
    domainname - set or display name of current Network Information
Service
    (NIS) domain

From Linux domainname manpage:
