an LSM volume. The filesystem took up an entire rz26 (c partition)
Later we mirrored this with a plex on a larger rz28. Now the 
original rz26 disk has failed. Having replaced it and failed to
get voldiskadm to rebuild the mirror we resorted to trying to do
it manually. Eventually it fails when I try to attach the new plex
to the remaining plex with :-

	Volume vol-rz2c, plex vol-rz2c-01, Block 0: Plex write
		Error: Write failure

I deduce from this LSM is trying to write to (write protected) block
0 and failing. I know most LSM partitions skip block 0 and start at
either block 1 or 16. On the otherhand encapsulated partitions dont 
seem to do this. I could adjust the disk label to make partition c 
start at 1 but I suspect LSM wont allow me to use the resulting
plex to mirror the remaining one because it will then be 1 block too 
short.

Any suggestions?

