We are in the process of migrating from ultrix 4.x running mostly on VAX's and
DECstations to OSF/1 (DEC Unix) 3.5/4.0. The C2 password security worked fine
in Ultrix and we were able to add Kerberos support. Now we find that
	1. OSF/1 does NOT support Kerberos (back to letting users use .rhost
		files - OH GOODY!)
	2. C2 is VERY SHAKY, at least on our AlphaStation 255. At least TWICE
		in the last few weeks a user (who is still in /etc/passwd AND
		in /tcb/files/auth/<first letter of username>) has been
		LOCKED out by login (but NOT by ftp) for no reason at all.
		In this situation EVEN root cannot reestablish a password
		you simply get

		cannot find userid

		or
	
		protected password (by whom? is there a root^2?)

Consequently, we have gone back to the Ancien Regime: NO C2, NO Kerberos, and
passwd encryptions in /etc/passwd -- at least we can login! Thanks a HELL OF
A LOT OS/F!
					Marc Thomas
					marc@ultrix6.cs.csubak.edu

PS: I'm keeping my VAXstation with Ultrix 4.x





