Mark Griffin <griffy@bigcat.fhsu.edu> wrote in article
<328CE815.30D9@bigcat.fhsu.edu>...
> I have been trying to setup Anonymous FTP on our DEC Alpha runnning
> Digital Unix V. 3.2.  ....

Yeah, You need to setup an etc and a bin dir in ~ftp

in ~ftp/bin put a copy of /sbin/ls mode 111 (Don't put /usr/bin/ls as it's
dynamically linked)
in ~ftp/etc/ put a copy of /etc/passwd /etc/group if you want you're ftp
users to be able to resolve file uids to usernames, gids etc. 

If your running base security, i.e. your passwords are in /etc/passwd you
may want to take the passwords out of the password file. I have these to
commands running in cron overnight:
cut -d: -f 1,3- /etc/passwd | sed "s/:/::/" > /user1/ftp/etc/passwd
cp /etc/group /user1/ftp/etc/group
This will keep your password copies up to date

Graham
