Depending on the access to 'at', you might be able to launch the
remaining script as a separate batch job within you script.  We do
something similar to ensure that overnight processing is not started
until archive processing is done.  Our command is 'at -f nightjobs now +
1 minute'.  If you need to create a dynamic (context oriented) job, you
can pipe the followup script into the job.  Just make sure you allow
enough time for the reboot to complete before starting the followup.
