Benjie Gandionco wrote:
> 
> I installed the patches for DU 3.2d that fixes the ping of death problem.
> After installing the patch TWICE, it still dies when pinged with a 64k
> packet.  Has anyone tried installing the patch?
> 
> --

First do a 'grep "3.2D" /usr/adm/messages'. The output will look like:

Nov 18 08:34:21 koibito vmunix: Digital UNIX V3.2D-1 (Rev. 41); Mon Nov
18 08:08:26 EST 1996

From this output, you can be sure whether you need the D-1 or the D-2 
patch. The tricky part is that you must install OSF360-350248 , before
you install the new ip_input.o file. That patch is included in the 
v3.2de2_ping_fix_plus.tar. So even if you have D-1 , you still need to
get both patch files.

Follow the instructions in the OSF360-350248 about copying files, but
do not rebuild the kernel. Replace the ip_input.o file from which ever
ping-patch (D-1 or D-2) is correct for you and now rebuild the kernel.

Note that it is very useful to make a copy of the /sys/conf/MACHINENAME
file to use for editing in any changes you might have done. As an
example
I had increased maxusrs from 32 to 64.

Hope this helps

Charlie

