If you use the C-shell (csh), you can limit the size of core files
that can be made.  For new users, I limit it all the way down to
zero.  Just put a line like this in your .login file:
     limit coredumpsize 0

Another way to prevent core dumps within certain directories is
to create an empty subdirectory named "core".  The kernel will 
not create a core file if this subdirectory already exists.
However, you would have to do this for each directory separately
that you wanted to protect from "core" files.

