gautam wrote:

> ...
> So basically how do we figure out where the unaligned accesses
> are occuring.
> ...
> 
> Gautam
One way to find unaligned accesses is to run the program under ladebug
(Digital's newer debugger). Compile the code with -g and then run it as
follows:

	$ ladebug foo
	(ladebug)catch unaligned
	(ladebug)run

When the program hits an unaligned access it will stop; and you can then
get a stack trace (assuming the stack isn't corrupt) using the "where"
command. You can then use dbx like commands to examine code etc.
-- 
- Anthony
(My views are my own; I do not speak for Digital and nothing I write
should be read as Digital's position)



