Jeff Denham (denham@zk3.dec.com) wrote:
: gautam wrote:
: > 
: > So basically how do we figure out where the unaligned accesses
: > are occuring.

Lookup uac in the man pages.

uac p sigbus

Then run your program.  It will core dump at the instruction doing the 
unaligned access.  Use gdb or other to view the source.

We usually go straight into gdb after enabling sigbus.  Then gdb
traps the signal and you're at the source line.

Curt Smith
