gdb has a -d flag ("man gdb") to specify additional source code
directories on the command line; within gdb, the "directory" command
("help files" will tell you all the commands useful for dealing with
files) manipulates the list of directories that are searched for
source code.

: Eventually, I plan to use gcc, but right now I am trying to
: enjoy using the taso and xtaso flags with the regular c compiler.

Don't forget to do the:
#pragma pointer_size save
#pragma pointer_size long
#include <stdio.h>
#pragma pointer_size restore

around system-supplied header files. Reading Craig Neth's advice on
"the perils of 32-bit mode" is advised: use AltaVista to search the
news for:

	+pragma +xtaso

if you can't find the article on your server.

