Benjie Gandionco wrote:
> 
> Is it possible to insert a system reboot in a crontab script?
> I want to do a reboot in the middle of a script and then continue
> right where it left off.
> 
> Thanks.
The only way I can think of implementing this type of action sequence
is:

	1) In your crontab script have the last two lines be like:
		touch /etc/LeftOffHere
		shutdown -r now

	2) In your system startup file/directory (depends on OS)
		In /etc/rc.local add a couple of lines like:
			if [ -e /etc/LeftOffHere ] then
				rm /etc/LeftOffhere
				# enter the pathname of the script to execute if
				# this circumstance is met or the lines to execute
				# to continue on with the original crontab script.
			fi

		In /etc/rc3.d create a script file similiar to the RC.LOCAL entry.

Hope this helps.

Jim Zahrndt (jzahrndt@cbsofil.com)



