Ran Zahor wrote:
> 
> Hi all,
> 
> I recently have a problem on the Alpha Dec 3000 600, DU 3.2c.
> 
> At first I got "vmunix: task table is full" message on the console,
> and the users got the message "no more processes".
> 
> I cahnge the maxusers parameter on at the Kernel from 32 to 64.
> I realized that maxusers affect maxproc and taskmax.
> After building the new Kernel maxusers didn't change and remain 32,
> and so the orginal problem.

How did you change the maxusers parameter? You should be able to use
sysconfig to alter the value of the task-max variable. You'll have to
reboot, but not build a new kernel.
Alternatively you can set the value of 'maxproc' in the kernel
configuration file and build a new kernel.
Changing the maxusers should work - but I can't say why it didn't
without more information.

You should also make sure that the task-max limitation is being reached,
not an individual's limit, but I believe this is the case.

Cheers,

Matt
