In article <55q13s$o3t@ratatosk.uio.no>,
Tarjei Jensen <tarjeij@ulrik.uio.no> wrote:
> 
> Anybody know of a utility for adding users in bulk? Soon I will have to add
> around 100 users and I don't fancy doing that with adduser.
  
There are a couple ways you could do it.  One would be to get the tool 
``convuser'' from Digital.  It's an unofficial tool available under 3.x --
at 4.x it's part of the OS.  convuser lets you convert users from base to
enhanced security and back.  Then it just becomes a matter of getting the 
users into the passwrd file and running `convuser' for each user you've 
added, to create the appropriate tcb file.

Another method would be to look through the adduser script and see what it
does and mimic that in a script of your own that's not interactive.

Tim
