In article <55l5h3$9jn@polaris.eurocontrol.fr>, Ollivier.Robert@eurocontrol.fr (Ollivier Robert) writes:
>Hi everyone,
>
>A friend of mine has a DEC machine with an NCR SCSI controller. I know that
>the adapter does support the "tagged command" feature (because FreeBSD can
>use it) but I'd like to know if the SCSI driver in OSF/1 does ?
>
OSF/1 or DIGITAL UNIX drivers support SCSI tag queuing. However it is not 
always used. DU needs to be told that a disk supports this feature before
it will be used. The definitions of DIGITAL disks is in /sys/data/cam_data.c
