Benjie Gandionco wrote:
> 
> What's the difference if I do a tar to these two devices?
> I noticed that using /dev/rmt0 is much faster, but it can only do small
> files.

The /dev/rmt0* come in different densities, which depend on the tape
device connected to your computer. If you use e.g. an EXABYTE 8505, you
would have:
/dev/rmt0h 5 Gbyte compressed
/dev/rmt0m 5 Gbyte uncompressed
/dev/rmt0l 2 Gbyte compressed
/dev/rmt0a 2 Gbyte uncompressed

In the original version of MAKEDEV, there's NO such device as rmt0. I
suppose there is a link to one of the devices given above, apparently to
rmt0l or rmt0a. The explanation should be similar for DAT drives.

Cheers, Torsten.


******
Torsten Hehl, Physikalisches Institut Tuebingen.



