Tim Antler (tantler@mdshealth.com) wrote:
: 	Has anyone ever encountered this before?  Is it a Digital UNIX quirk or
: Oracle.  We are running DU 3.2c. The backup/restore software is Polycenter
: Save/Restore that comes with DU.
We had a similar problem as we deleted the /oracle tree without shutting
down the database. As long as a process accesses a file, the space is
claimed even when another process deletes it and even if the file is not
in any directory anymore.

So, make sure all ora_* (...) processes are killed and the disk will
be ok.

