I originally had the following problem:

> Hi all Managers!
> 
> I recently have a problem on the Alpha Dec 3000 600, DU 3.2c.
> 
> At first I got "vmunix: task table is full" message on the console,
> and the users got the message "no more processes".
> 
> I cahnge the maxusers parameter on at the Kernel from 32 to 64.
> I realized that maxusers affect maxproc and taskmax.
> After building the new Kernel maxusers didn't change and remain 32,
> and so the orginal problem.
> 
> Thanks for your help in advance. 


Thanks to:
            Patrick Farley.
            Hellebo Knut.
            Benoit Maillard.
            Javier Aida
            Todd Acheson.
            Yehoshua form Digital Israel Support.                   

The steps that solve the problem was:

1. Edit the /sys/conf/SYSTEM kernel config file. Find MAXUSERS and
I         change 32 to 64. Save and exit.

2. Do 'doconfig -c SYSTEM'

3. cp /vmunix /vmunix.old;mv /sys/SYSTEM/vmunix.SYSTEM /vmunix;reboot

To see that the change realy take affect after reboot :

1. DO 'kdbx -k /vmunix /dev/mem'.

2. p maxusers. 
      
-- 
