|>Your upgrade went fine. You have a licensing issue. 3.0 did not check the
|>licenses in LMF (License Manager Facility). 3.2 does. You need to register
|>the Base PAK in LMF and any other software licenses you have (including
|>licenses for additional users) before 3.2 will let you log in. You
|>should have all the License Pak documents. Run LMF and type 'register'.
|>It will bring up vi with the blank template. Add the values on the License
|>Pak document in the appropriate places in the template (case does not matter,
|>and the Checksum is <digit>-<all alpha> (at least on all the license paks
|>I have)). Exit vi and the license will be registered. You have to do a
|>'reset' for LMF to start using the licenses.
|>

Clarification:  3.0 DID check the licenses in LMF.  This means that the PAKs 
were installed previously.  Ultimately, I believe that the PAKs had expired in
this case and perhaps 3.0 didn't appropriately handle that situation but 3.2
did.


